-- title:
--   Level automorphisms fix level-Γ₀(M') functions read in q^q
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\zeta$ be an element of `Idx q`, that is, a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. Let $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lie in $\Gamma_0(M')$. Let $g$ be a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ belonging to `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma0 M'))`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\!(T)\!)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the elements of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma0 M')`, the latter being the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(T)\!)$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g$ attached to weight-$k$ modular forms $f, g$ on $\Gamma_0(M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ and $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g \ne 0$. Let $x$ be an element of `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with $H$ the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, and assume that the Laurent series underlying $x$ is `qExpand (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q g`, the series obtained from $g$ by multiplying every exponent by $q$ (substitution $z \mapsto qz$). Then the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'` fixes $x$. Here `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is, by definition, a chosen automorphism $\tau$ satisfying `IsLevelAutBar q M' ζ γ τ` — namely: for every weight $k$, all modular forms $f, g$ on $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ of weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ and $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g \ne 0$, and every ring embedding $\iota : \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$, the $\iota$-image of $\tau(\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElem}\,q\,\gamma$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElem}\,q\,\gamma$ — and is the identity if no such automorphism exists.
--
--   This is the statement, in Shimura's theory of the modular function fields, that functions of level $\Gamma_0(M')$ pulled back along $z \mapsto qz$ are fixed by all the level automorphisms attached to elements of $\Gamma_0(M')$; no Borel-type congruence condition on $\gamma$ beyond $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ is imposed. It feeds the results identifying the elements of the full-level field fixed by all these automorphisms as exactly those of the form `qExpand` of a level-$\Gamma_0(M')$ function, such as [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_coe_eq_qExpand_of_forall_levelAutBar_apply_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_coe_eq_qExpand_of_forall_levelAutBar_apply_eq) and its variants for $q = 2, 3$.
